diff --git a/docs/api_to_audit.md b/docs/api_to_audit.md
index 059ff5b2d8e2533977199b6b756dcf31fd073599..f65816be5d091eeb793656b378aee691b4dfb89e 100644
--- a/docs/api_to_audit.md
+++ b/docs/api_to_audit.md
@@ -3458,6 +3458,27 @@ Ordinary native UI attribution and presence are separate capabilities.
 
 ## Plugin presentation compatibility
 
+## `bb.sdk.threads.experimental_contextMagnetContributions` and `bb.agents.configure().experimental_contextMagnetTrace`
+
+The trace reader is a thread-authorized, read-only walk of explicitly retained
+Context Magnet contribution facts. Pages are snapshot-bound and include
+retention boundaries, completeness, gaps, safe original/unknown evidence, and
+redactions. An empty page is not a historical claim. Consumers must use the
+supplied operation and rationale anchors and may not join provider/session/log
+data.
+
+The configure declaration is intentionally narrow: it accepts only a typed,
+bounded contribution declaration and the name of an explicitly selected
+receipt tool. It does not synthesize trace records from selected tools, skills,
+instructions, provider payloads, or generic configuration. The host assigns
+the contribution key and records consumption only when the exact receipt tool
+is invoked through a host-owned turnId/callId. Delivery and consumption remain
+separate.
+
+Before stabilizing, audit declaration lifetime and deduplication, snapshot
+expiry/pruning, cross-principal cursors, operation anchor rendering, receipt
+fan-out, evidence-body rejection, and SDK compatibility with older servers.
+
 `bb.experimental_p6rRoutes?.p6rThreadPath` uses the host's canonical project or
 personal thread path. The optional second HTTP handler argument contains only
 `experimental_p6rExternalOrigin`: configured `BB_APP_URL` origin, or direct
